Z||000004||Ken Wittlief||05-28-2001||10:39 AM||||The O2 sensor is the way the ECM decides if it should make th emixture richer or leaner - if its way off then you could be running lean.<P>  No codes?!<P>  if you havent replaced it in the last 30,000 miles and if you dont find any vacuum leaks then replace your O2 sensor - its only about$30 max - BTW the pipe needs to be hot when you take the old on off.<P>   the other sign of a vacuum leak is high idle - what is your idle speed when the car is in neutral and warmed up. If its over 1000 RPM you most likely have a vacuum leak.||||reg||1
